  "id": "prospective-validity",
  "term": "prospective validity",
  "definition": "Prospective validity is the extent to which a model’s or measure’s predictive performance remains accurate when tested on future cases in real-world prospective use, rather than only in past data. It concerns whether reported prediction results will hold up over time despite temporal changes.",
